## Summary
Add a JSON-based `repo-template` file to standardize new QhySync projects.  
This template defines the folder structure, essential files, and placeholders for project setup.

## Changes
- Added `repo-template.json` with:
  - Folder structure for `src/`, `tests/`, `docs/`, `.github/workflows`, `.github/config`
  - Essential files: `README.md`, `docs/README.md`, `.gitignore`, LICENSE, workflow, and PR template references
  - Placeholders for project name, author, and description
- Aligns new projects with QhySync developer profile and modular standards

## Testing
- Verified JSON structure for valid formatting
- Confirmed folder and file paths match QhySync starter repo conventions

## Notes
- This template can be used by automation scripts or GitHub Actions to scaffold new projects
- Ensures consistency across all Qhy-Projects
- Fully compatible with CI/CD workflows and QhySync AI PR note generation

